      m: `This goal is complete when two things are posted to the Troop 3054 portal: the annual program planning procedure, revised from the PLC's own review of it, and the program year calendar the PLC produces at the annual planning conference using it, with a start time and a location on every event. Changes the Scouts make to that calendar afterward do not undo completion.`,
      a: `Writing the procedure is mine. Running the conference is theirs, which is the point. Roadblocks: adults filling silences out of habit, and a PLC that has not planned at this level before. Mitigation is agreeing with the Scoutmaster in advance on exactly what the committee stops doing, walking the senior patrol leader through the procedure beforehand rather than correcting him during the conference, and keeping the ask to a calendar rather than a fully worked plan for every event.`,
      r: `The committee had been doing the Scouts' planning for them, which is the patrol method backwards. A troop where the Scouts build the year gets a program they chose and a dozen of them get real practice at planning something and being held to it. This is the change I asked the committee to make for this program year, and it is worth nothing if it depends on me being in the room.`,
      t: `Handoff agreed with the Scoutmaster by October 31, 2026. Procedure drafted and the senior patrol leader walked through it by December 31, 2026. PLC's post-meeting review running by February 28, 2027. Annual planning conference held, the procedure revised from the PLC's feedback, and both it and the calendar posted to the portal by May 31, 2027.`,
